                "text": "Let me understand the rule. Background azure (8). One non-8 pixel. Find closest corner (using Euclidean distance in verifier actually). Fill rectangle from pixel to that corner.\n\nNote: natural language says \"shortest distance in rows and columns\" but verifier uses Euclidean. Let me check with example: pixel at (2,1), grid 8x4. Corners: TL(0,0) dist=sqrt(4+1)=2.236, TR(0,3) dist=sqrt(4+4)=2.828, BL(7,0) dist=sqrt(25+1)=5.099, BR(7,3)=sqrt(25+4)=5.385. Closest TL. Fill [0:3,0:2]=9. Output matches. Good.\n\nI need to create 4 demonstration pairs. To teach the student, I should include diverse cases: each corner, different colors, different grid sizes, edge cases (equidistant? ambiguous). Better to avoid ambiguity, but including a case where pixel is in a corner region for each of 4 corners.\n\nLet me design 4 inputs, one for each corner.\n\nGrid 5x5.\n\n1. TL corner: pixel at (1,1), color 3. Distances: TL sqrt2, TR sqrt(1+9)=3.16, BL sqrt(16+1)=4.12, BR sqrt(16+9)=5. TL wins. Fill [0:2,0:2]=3.\n\n2. TR corner: pixel at (0,3), color 5 in 5x5. TL dist 3, TR dist 1, BL sqrt(16+9)=5, BR sqrt(16+1)=4.12. TR wins. Fill [0:1,3:5]=5.\n\n3. BL corner: pixel at (3,1), color 2, 5x5. TL sqrt(9+1)=3.16, TR sqrt(9+4)=3.6, BL sqrt(4+1)=2.236, BR sqrt(4+4)=2.828. BL wins. Fill [3:5,0:2]=2.\n\n4. BR corner: pixel at (4,3)? dist to BR sqrt(0+1)=1. Fill [4:5,3:5]. Hmm but maybe use (3,3): TL sqrt(9+9)=4.24, TR sqrt(9+0)=3, BL sqrt(4+9)=3.6, BR sqrt(4+0)=2. BR wins. Fill [3:5,3:5]=color.\n\nActually I'd like to use variable sizes to show generality. Let me make different dimensions.\n\nLet me also be careful that with Euclidean distance vs Chebyshev, for some positions the nearest corner differs. But we just follow verifier. I'll pick clear cases.\n\nLet me do:\n\nPair 1: 6x5 grid, pixel at (1,1) color 4. TL wins? TL sqrt2. TR sqrt(1+9)=3.16. BL sqrt(25+1)=5.1. BR sqrt(25+9)=5.8. Yes TL. Fill rows0-1, cols0-1.\n\nPair 2: 4x6 grid, pixel at (1,4) color 7. TL sqrt(1+16)=4.12, TR sqrt(1+1)=1.41, BL sqrt(9+16)=5, BR sqrt(9+1)=3.16. TR wins. Fill rows0-1, cols4-5.\n\nPair 3: 6x4 grid, pixel at (4,1) color 6. TL sqrt(16+1)=4.12, TR sqrt(16+9)=5, BL sqrt(1+1)=1.41, BR sqrt(1+9)=3.16. BL wins. Fill rows4-5, cols0-1.\n\nPair 4: 5x6 grid, pixel at (3,4) color 1. TL sqrt(9+16)=5, TR sqrt(9+4)=3.6, BL sqrt(4+16)=4.47, BR sqrt(4+4)=2.83. BR wins. Fill rows3-4, cols4-5.\n\nThese are all unambiguous. Good.\n\nLet me call show_transformed_input for each.\n\nI can call multiple in one block. Let's do so.",
